      {
        "id": 60460,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-20T15:07:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I tend to Timeshift myself to help speed up my set up, but one time I did randomly Timeshift Gloomy once during a game to see if I could get his last Relic out and dump it straight into the trash…and it worked :D.</p>\n<p>Any ability that lets you look at the top (or top two) card(s) of a deck isn't infallible, since you might always turn up horrible cards. Like Turmoil or an Infra-Red Eyepiece might turn up both copies of That Sodding Card in Citizen Dawn's deck, or EPEs in Omnitron's (though admittedly the latter can be dealt with if you have enough damage or something like Hypersonic Assault to nullify it while you work on destroying it). If no-one else after you has any means of manipulating the top card(s) of the deck, you're probably gonna be stuck knowing exactly what's about to come out and being unable to do anything about it.</p>\n<p>So it doesn't matter which deck-checking ability you're using, you <span class=\"bbcode-i\">always</span> have the risk that horrible cards will come out…unless they've already been, I suppose.</p>",
        "post_number": 78,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:36:31.159Z",
