      {
        "id": 60468,
        "name": "Oaktree",
        "username": "Oaktree",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-25T04:20:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Had an interesting \"Unity Experience\" tonight.&nbsp; Solo game pitting Mr Fixer, Unit, and Team Leader Tachyon vs. Advanced Baron Blade on Wagner Mars Base.</p><p>My experience with Mr Fixer so far has been sort of poor, so I was mildly worried I'd have issue getting the necessary damage to flip BB in time.&nbsp; Turns out that Fixer got Dual Crowbar, a good style, and Harmony out quickly and was gleefully pounding away at BB's devices and minions.&nbsp; Unity got a few bots out, a few more, and then lost a few to a Fire in the Biosphere and accumulating damage.&nbsp; TLT facilitated card draws, played out burst cards, and eventually flipped BB with a well-timed Lightspeed Barrage.&nbsp; This was also the first time I ever saw BB get all three MDPs out in the first half of the game.</p><p>Second half starts with Red Dust taking equipment and BB getting a Living Force Field out to raise his DR to -2.&nbsp; Fixer get equipment back out and I plan on switching styles so that he can make damage to BB irreducible for everyone else.&nbsp; Unity is low on bot cards, so she starts fishing killed golems out of her trash.&nbsp; Tachyon is back to discarding burst cards and helping people with more draws.</p><p>Environment plays a Meteor Storm.&nbsp; And then BB plays a Backlash Field.&nbsp;</p><p>That puts a crimp in things.&nbsp; Someone has to skip a turn to get the Meteor Storm (Tachyon out of her card for that, and no Bee Bots yet.)&nbsp; And even then, the Backlash Field is pretty much a bot-crippler.&nbsp; OK, we'll leave the Meteor Storm up for a round or two and see who builds up faster - BB or the heroes.</p><p>Turned out to be the heroes.&nbsp; A few rounds later (when a Bee Bot was available) Unity had something like eight golems in play.&nbsp; Fixer was ready to negate BB's DR, and Tachyon kicked off the show by skipping her turn to remove the Meteor Storm.</p><p>BB played an Elemental Redistributor.&nbsp; Then hit Tachyon for 4 - who redirected it to a Blade Battalion to take it from 5 pts to 1 pt.&nbsp; It then hit Fixer for 1 HP.&nbsp; Fixer played Overdrive - first strike hit a Bee Bot.&nbsp; The Bee Bot hit the ED for 2, then it nuked BB's Backlash Field.&nbsp; Dual Crowbar part of first strike hits BB for 1 HP, but now all hits on BB are irreducible for the rest of the round.&nbsp; Second strike from Overdrive hits BB for 3 and the ED for 3.</p><p>The bots then go to town on BB like bees on Henry Winkler.&nbsp; Turret Bot hits BB for 3 and Unity does a Powered Shock Wave to blast the ED and then BB for 8.&nbsp; She also plays an equipment card and then Bot-hacks Champion Bot into play.&nbsp; Cryo Bot, Swift Bot, and Stealth Bot don't do anything more, but two Platform bots and two Raptor bots are there and simply shred what is left of Baron Blade at that point.</p><p>The quick bot roll-out was actually faciliated by the Red Dust environment card.&nbsp; A Construction Pylon was already in Unity's trash when the card came into play, but discards to get rid of the card brought it back into play for her twice.</p>",
        "post_number": 86,
        "post_type": 1,
